  "provenance": "Manifest assembled from a direct inspection of the official CIFAR-10-C.tar (Zenodo record 2535967, MD5 56bf5dcef84df0e2308c6dcbcbbd8499, 2,918,471,680 bytes) during Week 1 verification: full tar member listing (19 corruption .npy files + labels.npy), per-file byte sizes, labels.npy structure (5 identical blocks of 10,000, uint8, classes 0-9), and per-severity sampling of the four required corruptions. The 50,000 x 32 x 32 x 3 uint8 shape for every corruption follows from the fixed 153,600,128-byte file size (128-byte npy header + 50,000 x 3072 bytes) and the official generation script (hendrycks/robustness ImageNet-C/create_c/make_cifar_c.py), which applies 5 severities x 10,000 images to all 19 corruption types. Labels verified to match the canonical CIFAR-10 test labels."
